; The M04 bench — WO-0080, the first bench of the M04 era. WO-0080 §0's own
; opening sentence, carried from WO-0038: "the scaffolding is the deliverable
; as much as the rows are."
;
; AP-xgmii_tx_64.md rows live here, by packet:
;   WO-0080  A1, A2 ASSERT, A5 NO-ASSERT; B1, B2, B4, B5 ASSERT; C1, C2, C3,
;            C4, C5 ASSERT, C6 NO-ASSERT (eleven ASSERT + two NO-ASSERT rows,
;            plus U1, the scaffolding smoke unit with no row id) — seven
;            files, ten %expect_test units
;   WO-0081  D1, D2, D3, D4, D6 ASSERT, D5 NO-ASSERT; E1, E2, E3, E4 ASSERT,
;            E5 NO-ASSERT; G9 ASSERT (ten ASSERT + two NO-ASSERT rows,
;            families D and E complete) — three new files (test_m04_d.ml,
;            test_m04_e.ml, test_m04_g.ml), six %expect_test units;
;            bench.mli/bench.ml extended by one function, run_frames, with
;            run_lengths re-expressed over it (§5.3) — the four landed
;            test_m04_{scaffold,a,b,c}.ml files unmodified (regression
;            witness, §5.2)
; When a packet adds rows, add its line — WO-0038's own dune header found
; the staleness this rule guards against (see test/xgmii_rx_64/dune's own
; history) and this header follows that precedent from its first commit.
;
; Depends on hardcaml_ethernet (the design under test — REQ-010's
; type-identity check does its job if the implementation's ports diverge from
; docs/specs/ifc_check/xgmii_tx_64_ifc.ml, WO-0080 §7). tools/precompile_
; check.sh's STUBBABLE set does not cover it (WO-0080 §16.2 item 5), so this
; directory is EXCLUDED from that harness by construction and CI's `dune
; build @default` is the only compiler that reaches it (ADR-0005) — which is
; exactly why WO-0080 §16.2 rule 1 (every [%expect] block empty, promoted
; from CI's own diff) governs every unit here.
;
; No hardcaml_waveterm: no unit in this round needs a waveform (WO-0080
; §16.2 rule 3) — the RV-0038 addendum D1 finding (J-dv_lead-0023) about an
; unread Waveform.create's elaboration cost is the reason this stanza omits
; it from the first commit rather than adding it and dropping it later.
;
; dv_xgmii, dv_xgmii_probe, dv_axi64_probe and dv_monitors are the
; DUT-independent machinery WO-0080 §5.1 measures the existence of, at
; ee47eee, by reading the committed file that establishes each: the
; link-partner's transmit-side decoder and frame/word builders (dv_xgmii),
; the XGMII sample seam (dv_xgmii_probe), the Axi64 drive seam
; (dv_axi64_probe), and the standing strobe monitor (dv_monitors). None of
; libs/hardcaml_ethernet/src/xgmii_tx_64.ml or rtl_snapshots/** was opened to
; write anything in this directory (PROTOCOL §10, WO-0080 §8) — bench.ml
; reaches the DUT's ports only through the field names SPEC-M04 §4.1 and the
; WO itself state, via type-directed record-field projection, never by
; naming the concrete module that defines them.
;
; No new dependency edge beyond WO-0080's own six: dv_golden is not named
; directly because Frame.fcs (dv_xgmii) already reaches
; Dv_golden.Crc32_ref; ifc_check is not a dependency because the bench reaches
; every port by field projection off Cyclesim.inputs/outputs (WO-0080 §7),
; never by naming Ifc_check.Axi64_ifc's types.
;
; ppx_hardcaml ppx_jane ppx_expect, matching test/hardcaml_ethernet/dune and
; test/xgmii_rx_64/dune — this is the one directory in this packet that
; touches Signal.t/Bits.t and needs Base's operators alongside Hardcaml's ppx.

